+// the draw's world matrix and light matrix. This is done only where the draw looks as those the
+// game's shadow pass was seen to issue: positions as attribute 0, three big-endian floats; uniform
+// block 1 of 64 or 256 bytes whose first three rows are the world matrix (skinned models have a
+// larger block of bone matrices: never left out); uniform block 2 of 512 bytes with the light
+// matrix in rows 3-6. The depth axis is not tested (a caster may stand between the light and the
